Z||000000||lou_dias||04-28-2001||11:30 PM||||OK, I just bought this 88GT and it had a bad EGR that would spin in place if I disconnected the vacuum tube.  The car ran cold for the 2 weeks I've owned it.  Then all of a sudden I don't have full power anymore.  Then the car ran hot...  Now the cat got clogged and I chugged home 2 miles @ 20mph with a glowing cat and muffler.<P>I know I need an EGR and cat...  What else might be dammaged.  There was lots of popping noises the whole way...  If I replace the cat, muffler and EGR valve...will everything be OK or is there more to it...?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||04-29-2001||12:27 AM||||Hey Lou!<BR>Sounds like you are running way too rich...<BR>Use a block off plate to eliminate the EGR if you don't get inspected...<BR>Cut out the cat and put in a straight pipe too...<BR>Then see what is going on, perhaps the temp sensor is bad for the ECM, making it think it is running cold, and causing a rich condition...<BR>If you need to get inspected, then replace the cat and egr, but find out if it is running rich or lean, and find the cause first...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||04-29-2001||01:36 AM||||o2 sensor is cooked too!||||reg||1
Z||000003||lou_dias||04-30-2001||09:11 AM||||So there is no damage to anything but the O2 sensore, EGR and cat. converter...right...?  Replacing that and everything should be fine..?||||reg||1
